---

`POST /v1/auth/organizations/{orgId}/connection-sync/retry`

Reconciles existing local intent. Takes no body and cannot change membership, roles or authentication policy.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.auth.retryOrganizationConnectionSync(input: RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.auth.retry_organization_connection_sync(input: RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncInput) -> models.OrganizationConnectionStatus
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.retry_organization_connection_sync(org_id: String).await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::OrganizationConnectionStatus>, Error<RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.auth.retryOrganizationConnectionSync({
  path: {
    orgId: "orgId",
  },
});
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon
from photon_api.rpc_generated import RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncInput

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.auth.retry_organization_connection_sync(
    RetryOrganizationConnectionSyncInput.model_validate({
        "path": {
            "orgId": "orgId",
        },
    })
)
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .retry_organization_connection_sync("orgId".to_owned())
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

